## Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully implemented Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js App Router project.

### Changes Made

**1. Installed Package:**
- Added `@vercel/analytics` version 1.6.1 to the project dependencies
- Used `pnpm i @vercel/analytics` as specified by the project's package manager

**2. Updated Root Layout (src/app/layout.tsx):**
- Imported `Analytics` component from `@vercel/analytics/next`
- Added the `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag
- Placed it right after the existing `<SpeedInsights />` component
- This ensures analytics tracking is initialized on all pages

### Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Analytics documentation for App Router projects:
- Analytics component is placed at the root layout level to track all pages
- Component is positioned inside the body tag for proper initialization
- No configuration needed - the component works automatically when deployed to Vercel
- The implementation is consistent with the existing SpeedInsights setup

### Testing Results

✅ TypeScript compilation passed with no errors
✅ ESLint validation passed (only pre-existing warnings, no new errors)
✅ Production build completed successfully
✅ All 46 pages compiled without issues

### Files Modified

1. `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
2. `pnpm-lock.yaml` - Updated with new package lock
3. `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component

### Notes

- The Analytics component will automatically start collecting data when deployed to Vercel
- No additional configuration is required
- The implementation preserves all existing code structure and functionality
- Analytics data will be available in the Vercel dashboard once deployed
